- if no delegations configured, error
- spawn server if not active
- if --ui/--browser/--web, open browser ui (later)
- `--continue (session name)` to continue other inactive session (later)
- intro/license header, ENTER to continue
- begin downloading judging model in background if not exist
- open template .jsx file in $EDITOR with commented-out instructions.

```jsx
import { prompt, without } from "@cutout/agent/prompting";

export default (
  <prompt model="mlx-community/Qwen3.6">
    Look this up for me.
    <without>Search Tools</without>
  </prompt>
);
```

- on submit - if judging is in progress, show model downloading
  - once model downloaded, log scoring info
- if a qualifying delegation is found, execute delegation if working model is downloaded. this is saved to file with path shown at top, incl. delegation info
- press ENTER to begin next prompt

@cutout/store wraps ~/.cutout/agent/store

- potential other commands:
  - open all documents in current history (how?)
  - interrupt (also ENTER?)
    - this will re-open the previous md file for further editing
  - hide editor to re-show previous result (ESC? or get for free)
  - modify config settings
  - ...

What core server APIs are needed?

download model
  SSE

send jsx
  SSE return w/ abort signal ? long polling?
  evaluate vs. execute
  events
    waiting
    tool calls w/ parameters
    thinking tokens
    output tokens

get, edit config
  loaded tools, instructions, classifiers
  allowed memory, thinking level
  and so on

possible endpoints:

GET,PATCH /api/options

GET /api/models => active models
POST /api/models/:name // (download if not exist)
PATCH /api/models/:name
  instances: 0, 1, 2 ...

GET /api/sessions
POST /api/sessions
  // new session
POST /api/sessions/:id/turns
  // new turn
